Phase 6.2b+c: live status, progress bar, timer, Stop emphasis, slow-run tip

Worker: Host.tick -> {t:'progress', line, loops, elapsedMs}. Engine: progressPercent(loops) ->
sink.status('Running… line N · P% · T s') (P% and line omitted when unknown), sink.progress({percent, elapsedMs}).
Shared: RunSink.progress?, Engine.slowRunTip?; new shared/run-progress.ts (RunProgress state, formatElapsed, no DOM);
the shell keeps a 250 ms paint timer that updates the running cell's footer in place (no re-render): after 1.5 s a thin
bar (indeterminate when the count is unknown) with "P% · T", after 5 s the Stop button gets .primary and the engine's tip
appears once per page load. English and Arabic strings in i18n.ts; styles in cells.css (reduced-motion respected).
NOT done: transferable rgb buffers. Measured in Node, 512x512x3 post: clone 0.40-0.47 ms, direct transfer 0.08 ms,
slice()+transfer 0.45-0.54 ms (no gain). Direct transfer would detach the buffer the interpreter still holds and re-posts
(Figures keeps item.rgb and re-posts it when the figure changes), so it is not safe without an ownership change.
Tests: test/progress.test.mjs (8: RunProgress timing and once-per-session tip, status text en/ar, shell + real engine +
fake worker with a movable clock, indeterminate bar, remount, worker progress messages). Runtimes 109/109, notebook 63/63.
Needs: npm run build:runtimes afterwards (worker.js, build-info.json).

